zmx #294: Daemon.deinit freed socket_path, which the caller allocated before the fork with another allocator (Daemon.init: "Caller is responsible for freeing all variables passed into the init fn"); every session exit aborted in libmalloc.
The daemon compresses its scrollback once output rests a second, as the app's renderer does (Terminal.compress): zmx never called it, so a long-scrollback tab's daemon kept every page resident.
A command naming a session a zmx 0.8 daemon serves runs as the bundled zmx-0.8 (forwardOld): 0.8 frames its header as a packed { tag, len: u32 }, so it reads our protocol version byte as a payload length and never answers. An app built for 0.8 that an update swapped to this binary called `zmx history` on its main thread and froze (1.2.3 to 1.2.4).
